    "updated_at": "2025-08-08T13:45:35Z",
    "body": "> Feel free to raise a csswg issue about that, preferably with a brief explanation of why it is needed (aligns with hardware? fits an Apple API?)\n\nI'm assuming this aligns with [`kCGColorSpaceLinearDisplayP3`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/coregraphics/cgcolorspace/lineardisplayp3?language=objc)\n\n> How about we do those two, and then consider `display-p3-linear` as it makes its way through CSSWG etc?\n\nSounds like a plan. @ccameron-chromium I assume since you proposed it that there is Chromium implementer interest, could you confirm?\n\nWho is the best contact from Mozilla to judge their implementer interest?\n\n@annevk please raise the issue on [csswg Github](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues) to motivate adding `display-p3-linear` to CSS Color 4.",
